<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nazi Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as NSDAP, National Socialist German Workers' Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nazi Party, the National Socialist German Workers' Party, was the far-right party led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> from 1921. Founded in 1920 from the German Workers' Party, it rose during the Depression to become the largest party in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> in 1932, and after Hitler became chancellor in 1933 it was made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s only legal party. It was banned after Germany's defeat in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nazi-party.jpg" alt="Nazi Party" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RsVe, corrected by Barliner. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parteiadler_Nationalsozialistische_Deutsche_Arbeiterpartei_(1933%E2%80%931945).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
